      "writtenOn": "2024-10-03T23:40:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "why \"1\" in vendor_data_pad[127]? Can\u0027t this just be:\n```\nu64 vendor_data_pad[128];\n```\nwhich will set the whole thing to 0?\n\nWhy 128? If the old way was 64*sizeof(u64) \u003d 512, why do you now need 1024 bytes? I suspect this needs to be consistent with ARCH_TASK_STRUCT_SIZE_MAX so 1024 is needed for that -- if so, then this should be declared as:\n```\nu64 vendor_data_pad[ARCH_TASK_STRUCT_SIZE_MAX/sizeof(u64)]\n```\nPlease move this to a separate patch that also gives an example of how and why this is used.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 244,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 244,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "beee9513e01cbb1dd4a1a497fa8a72967ffe82dc",
